Quoted legal source texts carry their own terms, recorded per vendored encoding
row in subjects/<path>/<subject-id>/encodings/<encoder>/SOURCE-LICENSE.md (see
docs/directory-conventions.md §4.1). A pointer row records no terms here: the
encoding it indexes lives in another repository and carries its own. Where a
subject holds its source text at the subject level rather than inside a row
(directory conventions §6), its SOURCE-LICENSE.md sits beside that source/ — the
two contracts/investment rows below are of that kind.

Attributions required by those terms are collected here as subjects land:

  sg/pdpa-2012 — Singapore Personal Data Protection Act 2012, and the PDPC
  Advisory Guidelines. The applicable source terms are UNDETERMINED; see that
  subject's SOURCE-LICENSE.md. No attribution is recorded because none has yet
  been established, not because none is required.

  sg/penal-code-1871 — Singapore Penal Code 1871, section 301, published by the
  Attorney-General's Chambers on Singapore Statutes Online. The applicable
  source terms are UNDETERMINED, on the same open question as sg/pdpa-2012; see
  that row's SOURCE-LICENSE.md. Unlike sg/pdpa-2012 this encoding reproduces its
  section VERBATIM rather than paraphrasing it, which is a material difference
  for whatever assessment settles the question. No attribution is recorded
  because none has yet been established, not because none is required.

  us/chubb-hospital-cash — the first row here whose terms are DETERMINED rather
  than undetermined, and therefore the first that records a real attribution
  rather than an open question. The synthetic policy encoded in this row is
  Appendix A, "ILLUSTRATION 1: SUPPLEMENTAL HOSPITALIZATON CASH POLICY", of:

      Oliver R. Goodenough & Preston J. Carlson, "Words or code first? Is the
      legacy document or a code statement the better starting point for
      complexity-reducing legal automation?" (2024). PMC10894687.
      https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10894687/

  That article is distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License
  (CC BY 4.0), http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ — verified against
  the PMC full text on 2026-08-31. The encodings quote the policy inline (inert
  style), so this attribution discharges a licence CONDITION and must not be
  removed.

  The text actually encoded is a modified variant printed at arXiv:2502.17638
  Appendix A.1, which carries arXiv's non-exclusive distribution licence and
  does not itself cite Goodenough & Carlson for the policy. We rely on the CC BY
  grant above, not on that paper. See the row's SOURCE-LICENSE.md for what that
  distinction does and does not settle.

  contracts/investment/yc-safe-postmoney — the Y Combinator post-money safe
  (Simple Agreement for Future Equity): six instruments and four Pro Rata Side
  Letters, together with the SAFE User Guide, published by Y Combinator
  Management, LLC at https://www.ycombinator.com/documents. The forms are
  deposited verbatim under that subject's source/.

      Copyright Y Combinator Management, LLC. Made available under a Creative
      Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 License (International),
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/legalcode

  The grant is printed in the first-page footer of every one of the ten .docx.
  Verbatim, from the US valuation-cap form (the other nine differ only in the
  copyright year: 2018 on the US side letter, 2021 on the three non-US ones):

      © 2023 Y Combinator Management, LLC.  This form is made available under a Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 License (International): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/legalcode.  You may modify this form so you can use it in transactions, but please do not publicly disseminate a modified version of the form without asking us first.

  Attribution here discharges a licence CONDITION and must not be removed. The
  licence is NoDerivatives: this repository deposits the forms unmodified and
  does not publicly disseminate a modified version of any of them. Whether an L4
  formalisation of the form is an "adaptation" under that licence is an OPEN
  question, recorded and not resolved; see the subject's SOURCE-LICENSE.md.

  contracts/investment/yc-safe-premoney — the Y Combinator pre-money safe (the
  "original safe"), four US variants and the SAFE Primer, introduced in late 2013
  and superseded on 2018-09-28. Y Combinator no longer publishes these; the
  copies here were recovered from the Internet Archive.

  The applicable source terms are UNDETERMINED. Unlike the post-money row above,
  these documents state NO terms: every header and footer part of all four .docx
  is empty but for a page number, there is no copyright notice anywhere in the
  text, and the string "Y Combinator" does not appear in any of the four. The
  Creative Commons footer was added to the safe in 2018, four years after these
  captures. No attribution is recorded as required by any instrument, because
  none has been established — not because none is required, and not because
  silence is a grant. The forms are Y Combinator's work and are credited as such
  here as a matter of accuracy. See that row's SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
